AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::addRewardToken()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when token is zero address
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
├── when token has no contract code
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when token is collateralToken
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when token is borrowToken
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when token is the reward pool staking token
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when token is already configured
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without duplicating it
├── when reward token list already contains MAX_REWARD_TOKENS
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
└── when owner adds a valid token below the cap
    ├── it should append the token to the end of the list
    ├── it should increase the reward-token array length
    ├── it should set isRewardToken to true
    ├── it should emit exactly one RewardTokenAdded
    ├── it should not call or validate the token's ERC20 methods
    ├── it should accept a contract whose balanceOf or transfer behavior is malformed
    ├── it should allow a previously removed token to be added again at the end of the list
    ├── it should not change market accounting or Convex custody
    └── it should remain callable while paused frozen or Convex inactive
